# .gitignore (repo root)
# ==========================================
# Scoped deliberately: `server/.gitignore` and `client/.gitignore` handle their
# own trees. This file only covers build artefacts that land at the root.

# The mongod binary that `mongodb-memory-server` downloads.
#
# CI pins this location via `MONGOMS_DOWNLOAD_DIR` (see .github/workflows/ci.yml)
# and caches it, because the library's own default — node_modules/.cache/... —
# is deleted by `npm ci` on every run. The same variable name is easy to reach
# for locally, and the directory is ~100 MB of binaries that must never be
# committed, so it is ignored here rather than left to chance.
.mongodb-binaries/

# Local production database backups must never enter Git.
server/backups/

# misc
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local credentials/configuration are never project source.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vercel CLI local link state. Not secrets (the auth token lives in the global
# ~/.vercel), but it is machine-specific and recreated by `vercel link`, so it is
# not project source. Deploys go through the GitHub integration.
.vercel/
